==Dutch==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nl|dum|mijn}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|mīn}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*mīn}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*mīnaz}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|nl|/mɛi̯n/}} {{qualifier|stressed}}
* {{IPA|nl|/mən/}} {{qualifier|unstressed; may be spelt {{m|nl|m'n}}}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-mijn.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|mijn}}
* {{rhyme|nl|ɛi̯n|ən|s=1}}

====Determiner====
{{head|nl|determiner|dependent possessive, independent possessive|mijne|contracted form|m'n}}

# belonging to [[me]]: [[my]]
#: {{ux|nl|Dit is '''mijn''' mijn.|This is '''my''' mine.}}

