===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|nl|dum|mine}}, from {{der|nl|fro|mine}}, from {{der|nl|LL.|mina}}, from {{der|nl|cel-gau|-}}, from {{der|nl|cel-pro|*meinis||ore, metal}}. Some senses are borrowed from {{bor|nl|fr|mine|t=explosive device}} and {{bor|nl|frm|mine|t=tunnel for sapping}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|nl|/mɛi̯n/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-mijn.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|mijn}}
* {{rhyme|nl|ɛi̯n|s=1}}

====Noun====
{{nl-noun|f|-en|+}}

# [[mine]] {{gloss|place where [[ore]] is taken out of the ground}}
#: {{ux|nl|Deze '''mijn''' is mijn '''mijn''', ga ergens anders delven.|This '''mine''' is my '''mine''', go excavate somewhere else.}}
# [[mine]] {{gloss|device meant to explode when stepped upon or touched}}
#: {{ux|nl|Deze '''mijn''' is mijn '''mijn''', ga je ergens anders opblazen.|This '''mine''' is my '''mine''', go blow yourself up somewhere else.}}
# {{lb|nl|historical}} [[mine]] {{gloss|tunnel used for sapping enemy defence works or lines}}
# {{lb|nl|entomology}} [[shaft]] dug by an [[insect]] [[larva]] in [[plant]] [[organ]]s, such as [[leaf|leaves]]

